# Making a Living: The Microeconomics of U.S. Mexican Households.

**Authors:** Tapia, Javier

## Abstract
Examines the microeconomics of Mexican American households in Tucson (Arizona) and Los Angeles (California), exploring factors affecting household organization and the dynamics of Mexican American households as part of a larger cluster. Case studies of four households support the discussion. Causes of conflict and family interests and objectives are discussed. (SLD)

